<title>UK: Russian Novorossiisk closed by high winds, swell.</title>
<headline>Russian Novorossiisk closed by high winds, swell.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian Black Sea oil terminal Novorossiisk was closed on Friday because of high winds and swell, a reliable shipping source said.</p>
<p>The 650,000 barrel a day (bpd) port, Russia's main outlet for Urals blend crude exports, closed at 0200 local time.</p>
<p>Black Sea terminals Odessa and Tuapse and Baltic Ventspils were all operating normally on Friday, the shipping source said.</p>
<p>--London newsroom, +44 171 542 6280</p>
